  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nAs of 1 PM CDT, skies are mostly sunny. Temperatures are warming \nthrough the 70s and 80s. Northwest winds 10 to 25 mph with gusts up \nto 35 mph are happening.\n\nThe pattern over the next 7 days highlights an upper level ridge \ninfluencing weather conditions over this CWA (warm and dry most of \nthe time), per ensemble clusters analysis. An occasional shortwave \nprogged to work through or over the ridge will affect the \nstrength/amplitude of the upper ridge and potentially introduce \nprecipitation chances. Currently, the best ensemble-models-based \nchances in the forecast for precipitation align with Friday night \ninto Saturday (a 20-40% chance of at least 0.25in of precipitation).\n\nModels prog an increase in low level moisture tonight which could \nmean some areas (terrain-influenced) see fog by morning, if winds \ndecouple enough with surface high pressure nosing into the region, \nand if low clouds don't form.\n\nNot presently seeing any strong wind/low RH combo's in the 7-day to \nbe concerned with. Just continued D3-level drought conditions across \nportions of the western forecast zones.",
